**Skip reason (all 7):** Every vulnerability is in MIPS MSA (MIPS SIMD Architecture) optimized code in `libavcodec/mips/hevc_mc_biw_msa.c`. These functions are registered exclusively via `ff_hevc_dsp_init_mips()`, which is only invoked on actual MIPS hardware with MSA support. The target binary (`build_test/ffmpeg`) is an x86-64 ELF — on x86-64, the x86 SIMD dispatch table (SSE/AVX) is populated instead, and the MIPS code paths are architecturally unreachable regardless of what crafted media file is provided.
